questions.explanation:
Logical followed here:

Consecutive perfect squares

Option 1: 36, 49**
36 = 6&sup2;
49 = 7&sup2;

Option 2: 20, 9**
20 is not a perfect square
9 = 3&sup2;

Option 3: 25, 16**
25 = 5&sup2;
16 = 4&sup2;

Option 4: 81, 100**
81 = 9&sup2;
100 = 10&sup2;

Hence, the correct answer is Option 2 .**

